---
// COMPONENT SCRIPT: Pure, active JavaScript execution space
const title = "Sydney Custom Quiet Routing Engine";
const pubDate = "2026-06-27";
const description = "Inverting network topologies using raster zonal statistics to map pristine backroad transit paths.";
const author = "Tom Thatcher";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{title}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:ital,wght=0,500;0,700;0,900;1,900&family=Space+Mono:ital,wght=0,400;0,700;1,400;1,700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
    <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>

    <script is:inline>
      const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('schema-theme') || 'dark';
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', savedTheme);
    </script>
</head>
<body>

<div class="system-frame">
    <div class="corner-tag top-left">SYS.LOC // 0x33S</div>
    <div class="corner-tag bottom-right">v1.04_ROUTING</div>

    <header class="schema-header">
        <div class="sys-status">
            <span>Graph Extraction: Spatial Inversion Engine</span>
            <span>Status: [ACTIVE_TRACING]</span>
        </div>
        <div class="title-group">
            <h1>inverting the city mesh</h1>
            <span class="scientific-subtitle">A PostGIS Approach to Minoritarian Lines of Flight</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="main-layout">
        
        <div class="theory-block">
            <p><strong>[ABSTRACT]</strong> Traditional spatial routing algorithms operate on a fundamentally reactive premise: they optimize for the shortest path or rely blindly on state-mandated majoritarian cycling lanes (Chronos). By defaulting to these pre-striated channels, they steer bodies into hyper-congested, high-intensity transit corridors. This project actively affirms a different vector—building a custom spatial graph routing engine designed to uncover the quiet, dark gaps within the urban heatmap, mapping smooth nomadic alternatives through the city grid.</p>
            
            <div class="highlight-box">
                // TOPOLOGICAL REBELLION: The city is a striated field of capture. To avoid the reactive herds of the main arterials, the graph engine recalculates spatial cost metrics to actively prioritize difference, solitude, and systemic low-stress multiplicity.
            </div>

            <h2>The Problem: Intersection Vertex Distortion</h2>
            <p>Early standard iterations of spatial analysis utilized naive point-based data sampling at graph intersections to determine street popularity. This created a profound "vertex trap." Quiet, isolated backroads that happened to terminate at or intersect a heavily trafficked arterial artificially inherited the high congestion scores of the major road. This structural feedback loop broke network connectivity, introducing false penalties that truncated completely valid, pristine cross-city routes. It was an engineering manifestation of bad conscience—allowing a single major corridor to poison the surrounding spatial lines of flight.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="spatial-canvas-container">
            <div class="map-wrapper">
                <div id="map"></div>
            </div>
            
            <script is:inline>
              // Center coordinates targeting Sydney [-33.8688, 151.2093]
              const map = L.map('map').setView([-33.8688, 151.2093], 13);

              // Sleek, dark-themed base map tiles matching the dual-spectrum system frame
              L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', {
                attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors &copy; CARTO'
              }).addTo(map);

              // Custom spatial point marker at a core routing destination
              L.marker([-33.8688, 151.2093]).addTo(map)
                .bindPopup('<b>Sydney Routing Hub</b><br>Network topology cost calculation node.')
                .openPopup();
            </script>
        </div>

        <div class="theory-block" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <h2>The Engineering Pipeline</h2>
            <p>To resolve vertex contamination and bypass the reactive traps of point-based sampling, the calculation was shifted from point intersections directly to the true spatial body of the road lines:</p>
            
            <p><strong>1. Polygon Buffering:</strong> Generated ~2-meter wide ribbon polygons from the raw road segment vectors (<code>sydney_edges</code>) to explicitly capture the physical footprint of each corridor and account for minor positional tracking inaccuracies.</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. Zonal Statistics Extraction:</strong> Sampled a high-resolution Strava cycling heatmap raster underneath the generated ribbon polygons, extracting authentic pixel mean values (<code>tiff_mean</code>) along the entire continuous span of the segment rather than relying on point coordinates.</p>
            
            <p><strong>3. Topological Database Injection:</strong> Uploaded the canvas data directly back into PostgreSQL, caching the unified values in a dedicated <code>true_tiff_popularity</code> column within the spatial database matrix.</p>
            
            <p><strong>4. Inverted Cost Calculations:</strong> Multiplied geometric line lengths by exponential penalty weights for high-popularity segments, transforming standard physical distance into an active psychological and environmental index:</p>

            <div class="code-container">
                <pre><code class="language-sql">{`UPDATE public.sydney_edges 
SET routing_cost = ST_Length(geom) * (
    CASE 
        WHEN true_tiff_popularity > 200 THEN 10.0  -- High Congestion Majoritarian Channel
        WHEN true_tiff_popularity > 100 THEN 5.0   
        WHEN true_tiff_popularity > 20  THEN 2.0   
        ELSE 1.0                                   -- Pure, Non-Regulated Nomadic Space
    END
);`}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <h2>The Results</h2>
            <p>By deploying <code>pgr_dijkstra</code> across the inverted cost topology, the graph engine successfully mapped out a fully connected, 69-segment cross-city journey. Instead of being funneled into glowing traffic hubs, the path intentionally skates through the silent interstitial folds of the urban environment—opening up an entirely data-driven framework for low-stress transit routing that actively affirms variation over standard efficiency metrics.</p>
        </div>

    </div>

    <footer class="schema-footer">
        <a href="/projects" class="return-node">← return to core schema index</a>
        <div class="footer-controls">
            <button id="theme-toggle" class="theme-btn" aria-label="toggle system spectrum">// invert_spectrum</button>
            <span class="system-status" id="panel-status">status // mapping_active_lines</span>
        </div>
    </footer>
</div>

<script>
    const themeToggle = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
    themeToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const currentTheme = document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme');
        const nextTheme = currentTheme === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light';
        document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', nextTheme);
        localStorage.setItem('schema-theme', nextTheme);
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>

<style>
    /* Integrated Dual-Spectrum Style System */
    :root[data-theme="dark"] {
        --bg-raw: #050505;
        --bg-canvas: #090909;
        --ink-stark: #ffffff;
        --ink-muted: #666666;
        --ink-ghost: #222222;
        --accent-orange: #ff4500;
        --accent-green: #00ffaa;
        --map-filter: grayscale(1) invert(1) contrast(1.1);
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] {
        --bg-raw: #f5f5f5;
        --bg-canvas: #ededed;
        --ink-stark: #050505;
        --ink-muted: #888888;
        --ink-ghost: #dcdcdc;
        --accent-orange: #ff4500;
        --accent-green: #00aa66;
        --map-filter: none;
    }

    html, body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 100vh;
        background-color: var(--bg-raw);
        color: var(--ink-stark);
        font-family: 'Space Mono', 'Courier New', monospace;
        transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
        padding: 20px;
    }

    @media (min-width: 768px) {
        body {
            padding: 40px;
        }
    }

    .system-frame {
        border: 4px solid var(--ink-stark);
        position: relative;
        padding: 30px;
        max-width: 1200px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        background: var(--bg-raw);
        transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .corner-tag {
        position: absolute;
        font-size: 10px;
        background: var(--ink-stark);
        color: var(--bg-raw);
        padding: 2px 6px;
        font-weight: bold;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-family: monospace;
    }
    .top-left { top: -4px; left: -4px; }
    .bottom-right { bottom: -4px; right: -4px; }

    header.schema-header {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        border-bottom: 4px solid var(--ink-stark);
        padding-bottom: 24px;
        margin-bottom: 30px;
        transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .sys-status {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        font-size: 11px;
        color: var(--accent-green);
        text-transform: lowercase;
        letter-spacing: 1px;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
    }

    .title-group {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
    }

    h1 {
        font-family: 'Archivo', 'Arial Black', sans-serif;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.8rem);
        font-weight: 900;
        text-transform: lowercase;
        line-height: 0.95;
        color: var(--ink-stark);
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        margin: 0;
    }

    .scientific-subtitle {
        font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif;
        font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.4rem);
        color: var(--accent-orange);
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin-top: 8px;
    }

    h2 {
        font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-transform: lowercase;
        color: var(--accent-orange);
        margin-top: 30px;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .main-layout {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 20px;
        margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .theory-block {
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color: var(--ink-stark);
        text-align: justify;
    }

    .highlight-box {
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-orange);
        background: var(--bg-canvas);
        padding: 18px;
        margin: 25px 0;
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--ink-stark);
        transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .spatial-canvas-container {
        border: 2px solid var(--ink-ghost);
        padding: 15px;
        background: var(--bg-canvas);
        transition: background-color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
        margin: 15px 0;
    }

    .map-wrapper {
        border: 2px solid var(--ink-stark);
        background: var(--bg-raw);
        height: 450px;
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    #map {
        height: 100%;
        width: 100%;
        z-index: 1;
    }

    /* Keep Leaflet interface highly visible but aligned with theme tones */
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .leaflet-layer,
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .leaflet-control-zoom-in,
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .leaflet-control-zoom-out {
        filter: var(--map-filter);
    }
    
    .leaflet-popup-content-wrapper, .leaflet-popup-tip {
        background: var(--bg-raw) !important;
        color: var(--ink-stark) !important;
        border: 1px solid var(--ink-stark);
        border-radius: 0px !important;
        font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
        font-size: 11px;
    }

    .code-container {
        margin: 20px 0;
        background: var(--bg-canvas);
        border: 1px solid var(--ink-ghost);
        padding: 15px;
        overflow-x: auto;
    }

    .code-container pre {
        margin: 0;
    }

    .code-container code {
        font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--accent-green);
    }

    .schema-footer {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        padding-top: 24px;
        font-family: monospace;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        border-top: 4px solid var(--ink-stark);
        background: var(--bg-raw);
        transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background-color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .footer-controls {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 24px;
    }

    .theme-btn {
        background: transparent;
        border: none;
        color: var(--ink-stark);
        font-family: monospace;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        padding: 0;
        text-transform: lowercase;
        font-weight: 700;
    }
    .theme-btn:hover {
        color: var(--ink-muted);
    }

    .return-node {
        color: var(--ink-stark);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 700;
    }
    .return-node:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .system-status {
        color: var(--ink-muted);
    }
</style>